[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-reference","page":"API","text":"","title":"API reference"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NonLocalMeans.nonlocalmeans!-Union{Tuple{N}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{AbstractArray{T, N}, AbstractArray{T, N}}, Tuple{AbstractArray{T, N}, AbstractArray{T, N}, AbstractArray{T, N}}, Tuple{AbstractArray{T, N}, AbstractArray{T, N}, AbstractArray{T, N}, Any}} where {T, N}","page":"API","text":"nonlocalmeans!(output, value[, precision]; patch = 2, neighborhood = 7,\n              h = 1, skip_zero_offset = false, channel_dim = nothing,\n              output_precision = nothing)\n\nIn-place version of nonlocalmeans. Inputs aliasing output are copied first.\n\nWhen output_precision is provided, it is filled with the estimated precision of each output sample, (Σ pⱼwⱼ)² / Σ pⱼwⱼ², treating the weights as fixed. The return value is output unless output_precision is supplied, in which case it is (output, output_precision).\n\nchannel_dim has the same meaning as in nonlocalmeans.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NonLocalMeans.nonlocalmeans!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NonLocalMeans.nonlocalmeans-Union{Tuple{N}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{AbstractArray{T, N}, AbstractArray{T, N}}} where {T, N}","page":"API","text":"nonlocalmeans(value[, precision]; patch = 2, neighborhood = 7, h = 1,\n              skip_zero_offset = false, store_precision = false,\n              channel_dim = nothing)\n\nApply non-local means denoising to an N-dimensional real-valued array using KernelAbstractions.jl.\n\npatch is the patch radius: an integer (same in every dimension), a Tuple of integers, or a CartesianIndex with one radius per dimension. neighborhood defines the search window and accepts the same radius forms, or a CartesianIndices of offsets relative to each sample, e.g. CartesianIndices((-2:2, 0:3)) for an asymmetric window.\n\nIf precision is supplied, it weights the patch distances and is used to compute the denoising weights. When precision is omitted, a unit precision array is used and only output is returned unless store_precision = true. With an explicit precision, the function returns (output, output_precision); output_precision is nothing unless store_precision = true.\n\nskip_zero_offset excludes the center sample from the distance computation when true. The weights are exp(-patch_distance / h), where patch_distance is the precision-weighted mean squared difference between patches.\n\nInputs must use one-based indexing. If channel_dim is an integer, that permutation is treated as the channel axis and denoised jointly using a single set of weights; patches and search windows then span the remaining dimensions. precision and any returned precision array have the same size as value (one precision value per channel and sample). With channel_dim = nothing (default), all dimensions are spatial.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NonLocalMeans.nonlocalmeans"},{"category":"section","location":"#NonLocalMeans.jl","page":"Home","text":"NonLocalMeans.jl provides N-dimensional non-local means denoising for real-valued arrays, with optional joint denoising across channels.","title":"NonLocalMeans.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Basic-usage","page":"Home","text":"using NonLocalMeans\n\nimg = randn(Float32, 64, 64)\noutput = nonlocalmeans(img; patch = 2, neighborhood = 7, h = 1)\n\nSupply a precision array when samples have different confidence values. Request estimated output precision with store_precision = true:\n\noutput, output_precision = nonlocalmeans(\n    img,\n    precision;\n    store_precision = true,\n)","title":"Basic usage"},{"category":"section","location":"#Joint-channel-denoising","page":"Home","text":"Set channel_dim to the channel axis to compute one set of denoising weights jointly across channels. Patches and search neighborhoods span the other dimensions:\n\n# `image` has dimensions (height, width, channels).\noutput = nonlocalmeans(image; channel_dim = 3)\n\nThe same keyword is available on nonlocalmeans!. Colorant arrays are also supported when ColorTypes is loaded.\n\nSee the API reference for complete function documentation.","title":"Joint-channel denoising"},{"category":"function","location":"#NonLocalMeans.nonlocalmeans","page":"Home","text":"nonlocalmeans(value[, precision]; patch = 2, neighborhood = 7, h = 1,\n              skip_zero_offset = false, store_precision = false,\n              channel_dim = nothing)\n\nApply non-local means denoising to an N-dimensional real-valued array using KernelAbstractions.jl.\n\npatch is the patch radius: an integer (same in every dimension), a Tuple of integers, or a CartesianIndex with one radius per dimension. neighborhood defines the search window and accepts the same radius forms, or a CartesianIndices of offsets relative to each sample, e.g. CartesianIndices((-2:2, 0:3)) for an asymmetric window.\n\nIf precision is supplied, it weights the patch distances and is used to compute the denoising weights. When precision is omitted, a unit precision array is used and only output is returned unless store_precision = true. With an explicit precision, the function returns (output, output_precision); output_precision is nothing unless store_precision = true.\n\nskip_zero_offset excludes the center sample from the distance computation when true. The weights are exp(-patch_distance / h), where patch_distance is the precision-weighted mean squared difference between patches.\n\nInputs must use one-based indexing. If channel_dim is an integer, that permutation is treated as the channel axis and denoised jointly using a single set of weights; patches and search windows then span the remaining dimensions. precision and any returned precision array have the same size as value (one precision value per channel and sample). With channel_dim = nothing (default), all dimensions are spatial.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NonLocalMeans.nonlocalmeans"},{"category":"function","location":"#NonLocalMeans.nonlocalmeans!","page":"Home","text":"nonlocalmeans!(output, value[, precision]; patch = 2, neighborhood = 7,\n              h = 1, skip_zero_offset = false, channel_dim = nothing,\n              output_precision = nothing)\n\nIn-place version of nonlocalmeans. Inputs aliasing output are copied first.\n\nWhen output_precision is provided, it is filled with the estimated precision of each output sample, (Σ pⱼwⱼ)² / Σ pⱼwⱼ², treating the weights as fixed. The return value is output unless output_precision is supplied, in which case it is (output, output_precision).\n\nchannel_dim has the same meaning as in nonlocalmeans.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NonLocalMeans.nonlocalmeans!"}]
